**Live acceptance, 2026-07-31:** ran a real two-module Tsuki session --
this package and `slssteam-ronin` both active, injected into the same real
32-bit Steam process (via a NixOS `bwrap`-sandboxed launch;
`ubuntu12_32/steam`) simultaneously. Confirmed via `/proc/<pid>/maps`:
`cloud_redirect.so` (LD_PRELOAD) and `SLSsteam.so`/`library-inject.so`
(LD_AUDIT) all mapped into the same process with no env-var collisions
(required a namespacing fix in Tsuki's `steamlaunchext.lua`, see
[[tsuki_multi_launch_extension]] memory). Both fully initialized: this
package's log showed transport hooks installed on slots 5/7/8,
`IsCloudEnabledForApp` hook installed, GamesPlayed CCM detour installed.
`$TSUKI_RONIN_RUNTIME_DIR_CLOUDREDIRECT/ready.json` was written with the
real Steam PID and a fresh timestamp -- the `runtime-file` evidence
carrier (RONIN-CLOUD-7) confirmed working against a live host.

Found and fixed in the same session: `Log::Init()` never actually read
`TSUKI_RONIN_LOG_FILE_CLOUDREDIRECT` -- it always wrote to its own
default `~/.config/CloudRedirect/cloud_redirect.log` regardless of the
host-managed path `interface.json` declares. Confirmed live (the log
existed and was correct, just at the wrong path); fixed to check the env
var first, mirroring `slssteam-ronin`'s `src/log.cpp`. This revision's
hash is the fix; not yet re-verified live (the fix mirrors the
already-proven `TSUKI_RONIN_RUNTIME_DIR_CLOUDREDIRECT` pattern exactly).
